From: Dominique Leuenberger <dimstar@opensuse.org>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 10:58:25 +0000
Subject: Define PyInt and PyString compatibility macros for Python 3.13+
Upstream: pending (upstream repo lacks Python 3 definitions when SWIG drops legacy shims)

SWIG 4.3+ eliminated internal legacy Python 2 compatibility shims
(such as PyString_FromString and PyInt_FromLong).
OpenIPMI_lang.i already defines PyInt_AS_LONG for PY_VERSION_HEX >= 0x03000000,
so add the remaining missing aliases alongside it.

--- a/swig/python/OpenIPMI_lang.i
+++ b/swig/python/OpenIPMI_lang.i
@@ -442,6 +442,10 @@
   return s;
 }
 #define PyInt_AS_LONG PyLong_AS_LONG
+#define PyInt_FromLong PyLong_FromLong
+#define PyInt_Check PyLong_Check
+#define PyInt_AsLong PyLong_AsLong
+#define PyString_FromString PyUnicode_FromString
 #define OI_PyString_Check PyUnicode_Check
 #else
 #define OI_PI_FromStringAndSize PyString_FromStringAndSize
